WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.170
A visitor told our school: the morning

2
00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:05.390
class does better than the afternoon

3
00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:08.370
class, so afternoon lessons should end.

4
00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:10.430
The averages agreed.

5
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:13.900
But the averages were hiding something.

6
00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:18.170
Today: how to read data claims carefully,

7
00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:20.850
and how to keep pupils' data private.

8
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.460
We looked inside the groups.

9
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:26.020
The afternoon class had most of the

10
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.500
pupils who joined this year, and many

11
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.640
were still learning English.

12
00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.320
Within each group, the two

13
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.020
classes scored about the same.

14
00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:38.150
So the time of day was not the cause.

15
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.340
Two things can go together

16
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.080
without one causing the other.

17
00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:45.100
Before you act on a pattern, ask:

18
00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.000
what else could explain it?

19
00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.900
Be careful with small groups too.

20
00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:53.010
A class of eight can swing a lot

21
00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.530
from one test to the next.

22
00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:58.480
One good or bad day changes the average.

23
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.450
Look at several tests before you judge.

24
00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:03.690
Now privacy.

25
00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.900
When I share results, I share the

26
00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.680
class picture, not a child.

27
00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.520
Marks, health and family

28
00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.160
details stay private.

29
00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:15.670
A ranked list on the wall can

30
00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.430
hurt a pupil for years.

31
00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.290
Use pupil numbers instead of names.

32
00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.350
Collect only what your question needs.

33
00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.880
Keep the list of names locked away, and

34
00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:29.560
delete the data when you are done.

35
00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:31.250
Quick check!

36
00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.700
Pupils who eat breakfast at

37
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.280
school get better marks.

38
00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:37.750
Does that prove breakfast

39
00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.090
causes better marks?

40
00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.260
Not on its own.

41
00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:43.290
Pupils who come early for

42
00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.210
breakfast may also miss fewer

43
00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:47.450
lessons, or live closer to school.

44
00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:50.680
Breakfast may well help, but the

45
00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:52.420
pattern alone does not prove it.

46
00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:55.690
A fair test would compare similar pupils.

47
00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.450
In the app, open the bias lab.

48
00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.240
See how data that leaves out a group

49
00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:05.060
gives unfair answers, and how fixing

50
00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.280
the data changes them.

51
00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:07.950
Your turn.

52
00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:09.860
You want to show parents how

53
00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.140
the class did in a test.

54
00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:13.810
What is the safest thing to share?

55
00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.810
The class average and spread, not names.

56
00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:21.290
Remember: look inside the groups, ask

57
00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:23.570
what else could explain a pattern, and

58
00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:25.450
be careful with small groups.

59
00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.300
Share the class, never the child.

60
00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.420
Try it yourself: find one claim with a

61
00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.180
number in an advert or a post.

62
00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:37.420
Ask what else could explain it, and what

63
00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.760
data would check it, before you share it.
